+## Result, in one paragraph
+For the unsoldered static law on the sphere with the exponential overlap, the one-site conditional is `P_h ∝ e^{βs·h}` with `h` the sum of the six neighbouring records. Its total-variation response to a change of the field is at most `β|Δh|/(2√3)`: the derivative of `P_h(A)` along a segment is `β Cov(s·Δh, 1_A)`, the indicator's standard deviation is at most `1/2`, and the covariance of `s` under any `P_h` has eigenvalues `L'(x)` and `L(x)/x` (`L(x) = coth x − 1/x`, `x = β|h|`), both at most `1/3` by series with nonnegative coefficients (ratios `6/(n(2n−1))`, `3/(2n+1)`) (W1). One neighbour moves `h` by at most `2`, so each coefficient is at most `β/√3`, the row sum is `α = 2√3β`, and `α < 1 ⇔ β < √3/6` (W2). Block 03's coupled random-scan chain, re-proved for the sphere with the maximal coupling of densities and a time-`t` bound, gives the finite-window comparison bound `|μ_Λ^ω(f) − μ_Λ^{ω'}(f)| ≤ Σ_x δ_x(f)(D_Λ b)_x` (W3). For `β < √3/6` the finite-window laws have a common limit on cylinder functions, the specification has exactly one infinite-volume static law, and it is rotation-invariant (W4). Freezing one site gives `|⟨s_0·s_x⟩| ≤ α^{|x|₁}/(1 − α)` in that law and on every torus (torus distance), hence `M_N² ≤ ((1+α)/(1−α))³/((1−α)N)` and `sup_k ⟨|ŝ(k)|²⟩ ≤ ((1+α)/(1−α))³/(1−α)` uniformly in the side (W5). With block 19: the kernel exists for `β > 3√3π/8` and cannot for `β < √3/6`; the band is open (W6).
